(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// Types made from specs and the objects C makes (queue 268; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 268\"; the user's"] [4 1 "// 262 DECISION (a)): PyType_FromMetaclass and its three entries (FromSpec, FromSpecWithBases, FromModuleAndSpec),"] [5 1 "// PyType_GetSlot, the relative offsets of PEP 697 (PyObject_GetTypeData, PyType_GetTypeDataSize, Py_RELATIVE_OFFSET's"] [6 1 "// members), PyType_GenericAlloc and PyType_GenericNew, PyMember_GetOne and PyMember_SetOne, ported from CPython"] [7 1 "// 3.14.10's Objects/typeobject.c and Python/structmember.c (the PSF's license, LICENSE.md)."] [8 1 "//"] [9 1 "// A type made from a spec is a pyi type (NewExtType: static to pyi, its instances of a layout of their own, so a class"] [10 1 "// deriving from it keeps a C-born value as a class deriving from a built-in type does) whose slots call the spec's C"] [11 1 "// functions, and whose methods, members and getsets are descriptors that call C or read the instance's memory. Its"] [12 1 "// instances are C-born: their memory is the world's (tp_basicsize bytes, malloc'd, the PyObject head first), their"] [13 1 "// handle is that memory's address, and their ob_refcnt counts C's references as a proxy's does (world.go). Python's"] [14 1 "// references are Go's: the Go value (cObj) is in the handles' maps while C holds a reference or a C entry is in"] [15 1 "// progress (as a proxy is), and once it is Python's alone and Go collects it, its type's tp_dealloc runs (on the C"] [16 1 "// world's next entry, as cbuf's free): the C memory lives exactly as long as both sides need it."] [30 1 "// tp_flags (Include/object.h)"] [43 1 "// fullyQualifiedName is _PyType_GetFullyQualifiedName (PyErr_Format's %N): module.qualname, the module left out for"] [44 1 "// builtins and __main__ (queue 270b)."] [54 1 "// metaCustomNew is a metaclass's tp_new other than type's (PyType_FromMetaclass refuses it, queue 270b): a C type's"] [55 1 "// own tp_new, or a Python metaclass's __new__, below type in its MRO."] [74 1 "// the slots' numbers (Include/typeslots.h)"] [115 23 "// Py_ARRAY_LENGTH(pyslot_offsets)"] [118 1 "// binSlots are the number protocol's binary slots by pyi's operator: the operator's and the in-place one's."] [123 1 "// alignMax is ALIGNOF_MAX_ALIGN_T (tools/pyi/capi/include/pyconfig.h)."] [128 1 "// cType is what PyType_FromMetaclass records of a type made from a spec (CPython's PyHeapTypeObject fields)."] [131 26 "// tp_name: the spec's name"] [134 34 "// tp_flags: the spec's, Py_TPFLAGS_HEAPTYPE"] [135 34 "// the slots the spec gives (pfunc), the inherited ones of a C base added"] [136 34 "// tp_members: the heap type's copy, offsets absolute"] [137 34 "// ht_module"] [138 34 "// ht_token"] [142 26 "// a static PyTypeObject C ready'd (queue 269): its handle is the C struct"] [143 26 "// the signature tp_doc begins with (queue 270b: __text_signature__), \"\" for none"] [144 26 "// tp_doc as the spec gave it (queue 270b), hasDoc whether it gave one"] [150 1 "// cTypeOf is the nearest type of t's MRO made from a spec (nil: none)."] [160 1 "// builtinSizes are CPython 3.14's tp_basicsize and tp_itemsize of the built-in types a spec may name as a base (on a"] [161 1 "// 64-bit build), for the relative sizes' arithmetic."] [190 1 "// ---- C-born objects ----"] [192 1 "// cObj is an object whose memory is the world's: its handle is addr. outer is the instance of a class deriving from"] [193 1 "// its type that keeps it (nil: none), the object C's pointer names."] [198 17 "// its finalizer's object: in no cycle (the object and its outer instance make one)"] [199 17 "// its managed dict (Py_TPFLAGS_MANAGED_DICT, queue 270b), made on first use"] [204 1 "// deadObjs are the C-born objects Go collected while C held no reference (their life's finalizer's, from the"] [205 1 "// finalizer goroutine): their tp_dealloc runs on the world's next entry (reapDead)."] [216 1 "// newCObj is the Go value of the C-born object at addr (its memory's, of ct's layout), in the handles' maps."] [229 1 "// asCObj is the C-born object o is or keeps (nil: none)."] [245 1 "// cHandle is the handle of a C-born object: its address, in the maps again (a count of 0: unowned until the C entry"] [246 1 "// ends) when it had left them."] [258 1 "// pyOf is the Python object of a C-born object (the instance that keeps it, else itself)."] [266 1 "// reapDead deallocates the C-born objects Go collected (outside any C entry, before the next one)."] [274 13 "// a new object at the same address (cannot be: the memory was not freed) or still C's"] [280 1 "// dealloc is the object's tp_dealloc (its type's, a C base's, else subtype_dealloc's: the dict its memory holds"] [281 1 "// released, the memory freed), run with a Go value in the maps for the natives it calls."] [310 24 "// an instance over a built-in base (queue 269)"] [316 1 "// subtypeDealloc is subtype_dealloc for a C-born object (Objects/typeobject.c): the dict at tp_dictoffset released,"] [317 1 "// the memory freed (tp_free, PyObject_Free); the type is immortal to the handles (its reference left alone)."] [329 1 "// objectFree is PyObject_Free: the memory freed, a C-born object's Go value out of the maps."] [341 1 "// writeUnraisable reports a tp_dealloc's error as CPython's PyErr_WriteUnraisable does."] [344 1 "// genericAlloc is PyType_GenericAlloc (_PyType_AllocNoTrack): basicsize + (nitems+1) * itemsize bytes of the world,"] [345 1 "// zeroed, the head initialized (a new reference: ob_refcnt 1), its ob_size nitems for a variable-size type."] [370 3 "// a class deriving from the C type: the instance keeps the object, its memory names the class"] [376 1 "// ---- calling C ----"] [380 1 "// ccallT calls the C function fn with pointer-sized arguments; its result as ret (TPointer, TSInt32, TSInt64)."] [409 1 "// cEnter brackets a slot's call into C: the error indicator cleared, a missing native's panic its error."] [410 1 "// Usage: defer cExit(cEnter(), &err)."] [429 1 "// objResult is the object a C function returned (a new reference, stolen), or the error it set."] [448 1 "// intResult is an int a C function returned, -1 with the error it set."] [458 1 "// cAddrOf is the handle C gets for o (a C-born object's address)."] [466 1 "// ---- the slots ----"] [468 1 "// slot is the type's slot id: its spec's, a C base's (inherit_slots), else 0."] [479 1 "// fillSlots makes the spec's slots the type's: each pyi slot calls its C function."] [483 39 "// a metaclass (queue 270b): its instances are pyi types, not wrapped values"] [487 27 "// a built-in base's (queue 269): each takes the instance's built-in value"] [606 2 "// __ipow__(other, mod=None): wrap_ternaryfunc's optional modulo reaches nb_inplace_power (test_misc's ipowType)"] [647 3 "// tp_setattr, the name a char * (slot_tp_setattro's older twin; xxlimited_35's Xxo_setattr, py-eval-1122)"] [670 2 "// tp_new: the spec's (a C base's), else object's (tp_alloc, object_new's checks); tp_init: the spec's"] [673 3 "// type's own __new__ (the metaclass's instances made by type_new), unless instantiation is disallowed"] [724 4 "// the base's __new__ makes the built-in value from the arguments (queue 270b), its memory C's"] [759 1 "// bufferWrappers are a C type's __buffer__ and __release_buffer__ (Objects/typeobject.c's wrap_buffer and"] [760 1 "// wrap_releasebuffer over bf_getbuffer and bf_releasebuffer; queue 473): a memoryview of the type's Py_buffer for"] [761 1 "// flags, and its release."] [789 1 "// argsTupleDict are the positional arguments' tuple and the keywords' dict (nil: none) of a vectorcall's arguments."] [803 1 "// callCObj calls a C-born object: its vectorcall (Py_TPFLAGS_HAVE_VECTORCALL, the function at tp_vectorcall_offset"] [804 1 "// in its memory), else tp_call (Objects/call.c, _PyObject_Vectorcall and _PyObject_MakeTpCall)."] [823 48 "// PY_VECTORCALL_ARGUMENTS_OFFSET"] [834 1 "// ---- PyType_FromMetaclass ----"] [836 1 "// specFrom is PyType_FromMetaclass (Objects/typeobject.c): the type of the PyType_Spec at spec."] [839 2 "// PyType_Spec: name, basicsize (int), itemsize (int), flags (unsigned int), slots"] [869 33 "// Py_RELATIVE_OFFSET"] [909 2 "// the bases (get_bases_tuple)"] [972 2 "// the metaclass (_PyType_CalculateMetaclass over the bases; queue 270b: a metaclass other than type, a C one made"] [973 2 "// from a spec over type or a Python one, whose instances are pyi types with their Meta)"] [994 2 "// best_base: every base must allow subclassing; the first is tp_base"] [1005 2 "// the sizes"] [1020 2 "// inherit_special (queue 270b): the base's itemsize and Py_TPFLAGS_ITEMS_AT_END"] [1027 2 "// the special offsets (special_offset_from_member)"] [1033 36 "// Py_T_PYSSIZET"] [1038 11 "// Py_READONLY"] [1040 15 "// Py_READONLY | Py_RELATIVE_OFFSET"] [1057 2 "// a layout pyi can make: object's, or a type made from a spec, extended"] [1061 18 "// a Python class (queue 270b): its instances' layout is its base's, with a managed dict"] [1065 10 "// object's, a C type's, (queue 269) a mirrored built-in's, or (queue 270b) type's, int's, an exception's"] [1067 3 "// a spec that adds nothing over such a base (basicsize and itemsize 0, no slot but the doc's and the bases'): the"] [1068 3 "// heap subclass the metaclass makes of the bases, its instances the base's own (py-eval-1122: xxlimited's Str"] [1069 3 "// over str)"] [1101 18 "// queue 270b: Py_SET_TYPE(res, metaclass)"] [1106 2 "// the managed dict and weak references (Py_TPFLAGS_MANAGED_DICT, MANAGED_WEAKREF): the spec's, a C base's, and a"] [1107 2 "// Python class's (queue 270b)"] [1118 2 "// inherit_slots: a C base's slots first, then the spec's own"] [1144 4 "// the members moved to the heap type, their relative offsets made absolute"] [1159 17 "// Py_TP_USE_SPEC is NULL: the spec itself (queue 270b)"] [1168 2 "// check_basicsize_includes_size_and_offsets (for the generic allocator)"] [1184 2 "// the type's dict: __module__, __doc__, the methods, members and getsets, the sizes"] [1207 1 "// textSignature is _PyType_GetTextSignatureFromInternalDoc: the \"(sig)\" of a tp_doc that begins with \"name(sig)\\n--\\n\\n\""] [1208 1 "// (\"\" for none)."] [1221 1 "// docWithoutSignature is _PyType_DocWithoutSignature: tp_doc less its \"name(sig)\\n--\\n\\n\" signature."] [1234 1 "// addCMethods puts the PyMethodDefs of the table at defs in the type's dict: methods bound to the instance (self"] [1235 1 "// first), class methods (METH_CLASS) and static methods (METH_STATIC); METH_METHOD's get the type as defining_class."] [1245 33 "// METH_STATIC: no self"] [1263 13 "// a slot wrapper's name: the first one stays (METH_COEXIST not set)"] [1270 1 "// addCMembers makes each member of the type's tp_members a member descriptor reading or writing the instance's"] [1271 1 "// memory (PyMember_GetOne, PyMember_SetOne); __dictoffset__ and __weaklistoffset__ are the type's sizes instead."] [1292 31 "// not Py_READONLY"] [1305 1 "// addCGetSets makes each PyGetSetDef (name, get, set, doc, closure) of the table at defs a getset descriptor that"] [1306 1 "// calls C."] [1338 1 "// ---- PyMember_GetOne, PyMember_SetOne (Python/structmember.c) ----"] [1340 1 "// memberGet is PyMember_GetOne for the PyMemberDef at mb over the object at addr."] [1348 11 "// Py_T_BOOL"] [1350 10 "// Py_T_BYTE"] [1352 10 "// Py_T_UBYTE"] [1354 10 "// Py_T_SHORT"] [1356 11 "// Py_T_USHORT"] [1358 10 "// Py_T_INT"] [1360 11 "// Py_T_UINT"] [1362 18 "// Py_T_LONG, Py_T_LONGLONG, Py_T_PYSSIZET"] [1364 15 "// Py_T_ULONG, Py_T_ULONGLONG"] [1366 10 "// Py_T_FLOAT"] [1368 10 "// Py_T_DOUBLE"] [1370 10 "// Py_T_STRING"] [1375 11 "// Py_T_STRING_INPLACE"] [1377 10 "// Py_T_CHAR"] [1379 10 "// _Py_T_OBJECT"] [1384 11 "// Py_T_OBJECT_EX"] [1394 11 "// _Py_T_NONE"] [1408 1 "// memberSet is PyMember_SetOne for the PyMemberDef at mb over the object at addr (v nil: delete)."] [1448 11 "// Py_T_BOOL"] [1458 23 "// Py_T_BYTE, Py_T_UBYTE, Py_T_SHORT, Py_T_USHORT, P